A dereference applied to a call's result -- `*f(args)`.

Three faults in one shape, all on the path tcc uses to write every byte of
.eh_frame. Case 105 covers all three and was KNOWN GAP; it now passes on both
architectures.

    #define dwarf_data1(s,data) \
        (*(uint8_t*)section_ptr_add((s), 1) = (data))     tccdbg.c:550

1. THE PENDING `*` LANDED ON THE ARGUMENT.

primary_expr_variable eats the stars and parks the count in
num_dereference_after_postfix for the postfix walk to apply. For a function
designator it then returns early --

    int is_function = options & TLO_FUNCTION;
    if(is_prefix_operator || is_postfix_operator || is_indexed_local_array
       || is_function) return;

-- without clearing the count. The argument list is parsed after that point and
every argument is a full expression reading the same global, so `*give(8)`
emitted

    mov_rax, %8                  # primary expr number
    movsx_rax,DWORD_PTR_[rax]    # dereferencing the literal 8 as an address
    push_rax                     # function argument

and the call's result was never dereferenced at all.

The count belongs to the expression that parked it and never to a
sub-expression, so function_call holds it across the argument list and clears
the global for that region. It saves the CURRENT value rather than restoring a
constant, which is what makes it safe on the paths that deliberately consume
the count first -- see the `CONSUMED HERE` note in primary_expr_variable. Those
arrive with 0 and leave with 0.

EXPERIMENT-zzzg wrapped the whole call instead and went 12/12 -> 0/12. The
region that must not see the count is the argument list alone.

2. THE RETURN TYPE DID NOT REACH current_target.

primary_expr has a fast path that calls function_call(variable, FALSE) with the
symbol in hand, and function_call uses it to set current_target at the end.
Under a leading `*` that path does not match -- it tests global_token->s, which
is `*` -- so the call arrives through function_call(NULL, TRUE) with no symbol
and the result kept the generic function_pointer type. The dereference then
read at the WRONG WIDTH:

    unsigned char* give(int);
    *give(8)   ->  movsx_rax,DWORD_PTR_[rax]     four bytes, signed
                   wanted movzx_rax,BYTE_PTR_[rax]

That is a silent wrong VALUE rather than a fault, and it hides: the bytes after
a correct one are usually zero, so the wrong-width load returns the right
answer. Case 105 already guarded against this -- it sets buf[9] = 66 before
reading buf[8] -- but the minimal probe written while chasing fault 1 did not,
and it PASSED with fix 1 alone until 0xAA 0xBB 0xCC were written after the
byte under test. Third time this series has recorded that trap, and the first
where the case suite was already right and the throwaway probe was not.

The designator is recorded ONLY when a '(' follows, so `p = give;` cannot park
a symbol for a later indirect call to collect, and function_call takes it into
a local before parsing arguments so a nested `*other(3)` cannot overwrite it.

3. `*f(x) = v` LOADED THROUGH THE RETURNED POINTER.

The assigning branch loads once to turn an lvalue into the address being stored
through. That is right for a variable, where the register holds the address of
the SLOT --

    lea_rax,[r13-8]      address of the slot holding p
    mov_rax,[rax]        p's VALUE, the destination

-- and one step too far for a call, where the pointer is already in the
register:

    call_rax             rax = &buf[16]
    mov_rax,[rax]        loads buf[16..23] and stores through THAT

so `*give(16) = 99` wrote to whatever eight bytes sat at buf[16]. Only the
first level is spared: `**f() = v` still has to load once to reach the inner
pointer. Same rule as zzc, zzg, zzm and zzo -- an address applies to the last
step of a chain, never to a step that still has to be followed.

WHAT THIS DOES NOT DO, MEASURED RATHER THAN ASSUMED.

It does not close the heap corruption. Over the tests2 00_assignment shape,
swept across 24 filename lengths -- see tools/layout-sweep.sh, and the reason
that is the right instrument is below -- realloc failures fall from 15/24 to
8/24 and the compile still never succeeds. The corruption is confirmed to come
from the .eh_frame path by toggling TCC_EH_FRAME, which takes realloc failures
to 0/24 for this patch AND for the unpatched series; a second, independent
SIGSEGV remains at every layout in both. Neither blocker is closed here.

THE MEASUREMENT NOTE THAT MATTERS MORE THAN THE PATCH. Whether a given compile
survives depends on the length of its own FILENAME:

    a.c ab.c abc.c          rc=0    compiles
    abcd.c ... abcdefgh.c   rc=1    realloc: pointer was never returned

Identical bytes, identical binary. The filename is stored on the heap, so its
length shifts every later allocation and decides whether the stray write lands
on a live allocator node. A single compile is therefore one sample from a
distribution, and bisecting the INPUT finds filename lengths rather than
language constructs. Two conclusions drawn during this work were withdrawn for
exactly that reason.

GATES: difftest 89 pass / 0 fail on aarch64 and 87 / 0 on amd64 with case 105
closed, the stage-2 corpus unchanged at 419/426, and the twelve end-to-end
programs still 12/12 -- which is the one gate that compiles tcc, and the one
zzzg broke.

